
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>

    <!--
      Centralized warning-suppression policy.
      Full rationale + per-category removal criteria + follow-on tracking:
      docs/assessments/bff-warning-suppression-analysis-2026-06-01.md

      WarningsNotAsErrors: downgrades these specific codes from build-blocking errors
      back to non-blocking warnings (still visible in build output). The list is
      currently EMPTY.

      CS0618 (use of an [Obsolete] member) is a build ERROR again — re-armed 2026-11-11
      (reuse-governance-tightening-r1 task 042). Marking a member [Obsolete] therefore
      fails the build at every existing caller: the change that adds the marker must
      migrate those callers, or give the attribute a DiagnosticId (e.g. SPRK001) and
      suppress only that ID, at the call site or here, with a one-line reason. Never
      re-add CS0618 itself to WarningsNotAsErrors / NoWarn or as a file-wide pragma.
      REMOVED from the allowlist 2026-08-15 (quality-r3-followups):
        CS0109 — the single test site (UploadIntegrationTests.cs, unnecessary `new`) was
                 FIXED; 0 instances remain. Re-arms the gate.
        CS1998 — 0 instances solution-wide (already remediated); dead suppression removed.
        CS8601 + CS8604 — the NRE-risk nullable class. All 8 production sites (AgentEndpoints
                 optional Description, CommunicationService attachment name, SignalRDelivery
                 negotiate fail-loud guard, TodoGeneration guarded _dataverse!) + 3 test sites
                 were FIXED (not suppressed); 0 instances remain solution-wide, so the
                 suppression is dead and the gate is now armed against new null-reference warnings.

      NU1903 NoWarn REMOVED 2026-08-11 (dotnet-10-upgrade-r1 task 004, owner-approved Option 1).
      The original comment claimed NU1903 only masked the already-fixed Kiota 1.21.2 CVE — that was FALSE:
      it was ALSO masking System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 8.0.2 (8 HIGH advisories) transitive in
      Core/Dataverse/Scheduling. Both are now genuinely remediated: (1) the 7 Microsoft.Kiota.* 1.22.0
      direct pins in Sprk.Bff.Api clear the Kiota CVE (resolved graph has no 1.21.x); (2) the 3 shared libs
      now pin System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 10.0.11 (non-vulnerable). Verified: clean restore reports
      ZERO NU1903 with the suppression gone. Graph 5->6 / Kiota 1->2 is the separate task 033.
    -->
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
